## Additional Rust Best Practices

- Prefer `const` / `const fn` for compile-time constants and pure constructors.
- Use `matches!` macro for concise boolean predicates.
- Prefer `slice::sort_by` / `sort_by_key` over hand-rolled sorts unless a specialized O(n) algorithm is required.
- Use `std::mem::take` / `std::mem::replace` to leave valid dummy state when moving out of `&mut T`.
- Prefer `enum` with variants over `bool` + parallel fields when states are mutually exclusive.
- Use `#[non_exhaustive]` on public enums that may grow variants.
- Gate platform-specific code with `#[cfg(target_os = "...")]` and document supported targets.
- For I/O: prefer `std::io::Read` / `Write` traits and `BufReader` / `BufWriter` for efficiency.
- Format strings with `format!`, `write!`, `writeln!` — not manual concatenation in hot paths.
- When adding features, update `todo.md` or project docs only if the user requests it.
